Why don't you want me, huh?

277
00:22:17,878 --> 00:22:19,129
I could make you happy!

278
00:22:19,212 --> 00:22:21,214
- [straining]
- I could make our daughter happy.

279
00:22:21,298 --> 00:22:22,466
Why don't you want me, huh?

280
00:22:22,549 --> 00:22:24,968
Why are you fighting me, huh?

281
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:32,934
[both grunting]

282
00:22:35,437 --> 00:22:37,647
I would have given you a great life.

283
00:22:41,735 --> 00:22:42,694
[grunts]

284
00:22:42,778 --> 00:22:44,404
You're gonna kill me, huh?

285
00:22:44,488 --> 00:22:45,530
Then  go ahead.

286
00:22:49,493 --> 00:22:51,620
[groaning]

287
00:22:58,919 --> 00:23:01,296
[Ramon wheezing]

288
00:23:02,839 --> 00:23:03,673
[coughs]

289
00:23:11,014 --> 00:23:11,932
Oh?

290
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:19,397
[Ramon groans]

291
00:23:40,001 --> 00:23:42,129
Your friends, you know…

292
00:23:42,212 --> 00:23:44,256
You know, I ate them all.

293
00:23:46,216 --> 00:23:47,551
Let's go back home, Rebecca.

294
00:23:47,634 --> 00:23:48,927
[gun cocks]

295
00:23:53,557 --> 00:23:55,851
[breathes heavily]

296
00:23:57,769 --> 00:23:58,812
[screams]

297
00:23:58,895 --> 00:23:59,896
[gunshot]

298
00:24:03,441 --> 00:24:04,860
[Sabina yelling] Ma?

299
00:24:07,487 --> 00:24:08,405
Ma!

300
00:24:12,534 --> 00:24:13,952
[somber music playing]

301
00:24:24,462 --> 00:24:26,173
Ma! Are you okay?

302
00:24:26,256 --> 00:24:27,299
Aunt Becca!

303
00:24:28,508 --> 00:24:29,634
- Hey.
- Ma!

304
00:24:30,385 --> 00:24:31,595
Ma, wake up.

305
00:24:32,262 --> 00:24:33,263
Ma…

306
00:24:34,139 --> 00:24:35,557
Can you hear me?

307
00:24:40,770 --> 00:24:42,022
Where does it hurt?

308
00:24:43,732 --> 00:24:44,858
[crying]

309
00:24:44,941 --> 00:24:46,776
What happened?

310
00:24:46,860 --> 00:24:47,903
Are you okay, Ma?

311
00:24:47,986 --> 00:24:49,029
Tell me where it hurts.

312
00:24:59,789 --> 00:25:00,707
Bulak!

313
00:25:11,051 --> 00:25:12,135
Let's end this now.

314
00:25:14,554 --> 00:25:16,473
[creature screeches]

315
00:25:19,392 --> 00:25:21,353
[creature screeches]

316
00:25:25,148 --> 00:25:26,816
[leaves rustling]

317
00:25:28,818 --> 00:25:30,862
[Javier groaning]

318
00:25:37,285 --> 00:25:38,912
[groaning]

319
00:25:44,751 --> 00:25:45,752
Diwa?

320
00:25:48,296 --> 00:25:49,506
[Javier wheezes]

321
00:25:51,466 --> 00:25:52,676
What the hell?

322
00:25:57,055 --> 00:25:58,974
- We need to get to the boat.
- Yeah.

323
00:26:00,058 --> 00:26:01,476
Come on, we need to go. Now.

324
00:26:05,355 --> 00:26:06,231
[Rebecca] This way.

325
00:26:12,279 --> 00:26:14,155
Don't listen to the voices, Sabina.

326
00:26:17,075 --> 00:26:18,410
[Bulak] This place is so confusing.

327
00:26:22,038 --> 00:26:23,957
[Rebecca] Don't give in to the island.

328
00:26:27,127 --> 00:26:30,213
[rustling]

329
00:26:30,964 --> 00:26:31,840
Sabina!

330
00:26:39,055 --> 00:26:40,932
[Sabina] It feels like
we've passed here before.

331
00:26:41,016 --> 00:26:42,976
[Rebecca] The island
is trying to confuse us.

332
00:26:49,607 --> 00:26:52,193
[Rebecca groaning]

333
00:27:02,537 --> 00:27:03,413
[Bulak] Sabina!

334
00:27:10,962 --> 00:27:13,006
What is it? Come on.

335
00:27:14,174 --> 00:27:15,133
Go on ahead now.

336
00:27:17,093 --> 00:27:18,178
We're not leaving you.

337
00:27:19,054 --> 00:27:21,848
Tela was right.
The island won't let me leave.

338
00:27:22,766 --> 00:27:23,808
I need to stay here.

339
00:27:25,101 --> 00:27:26,561
You know that this has to happen,

340
00:27:26,644 --> 00:27:28,104
you just don't want to admit it.

341
00:27:31,149 --> 00:27:33,568
I don't understand
what you're talking about.

342
00:27:34,944 --> 00:27:35,945
Aunt Becca?

343
00:27:37,072 --> 00:27:39,407
Either I stay or we all have to stay.

344
00:27:40,241 --> 00:27:42,786
The island is calling to me, Ma, not you.

345
00:27:43,495 --> 00:27:46,289
I used to hate it when Uncle Art
would always tell me that,

346
00:27:46,373 --> 00:27:47,707
but now I understand.

347
00:27:48,249 --> 00:27:50,168
That's why you left without a word,

348
00:27:50,251 --> 00:27:51,753
why you covered your tracks,

349
00:27:51,836 --> 00:27:53,797
and why you forbade me to come here.

350
00:27:55,215 --> 00:27:58,593
I came from this island
and now I need to end this alone.

351
00:27:59,260 --> 00:28:00,762
The island always said

352
00:28:01,471 --> 00:28:03,890
the same blood runs through our veins.

353
00:28:05,308 --> 00:28:06,601
Aunt Becca, do something.

354
00:28:06,684 --> 00:28:09,729
[Sabina] One has to remain
and one must be sacrificed.

355
00:28:09,813 --> 00:28:13,650
If you could come back, Ma,
I could come back too. We're the same.

356
00:28:14,901 --> 00:28:16,736
You know this is the only way.

357
00:28:17,404 --> 00:28:19,239
Now, Bulak, hey. Listen.

358
00:28:19,322 --> 00:28:20,865
Take care of Ma for me.

359
00:28:22,534 --> 00:28:23,451
No.

360
00:28:23,952 --> 00:28:25,036
Not without you.

361
00:28:27,872 --> 00:28:29,207
We'll see each other again.

362
00:28:52,230 --> 00:28:54,399
[panting]

363
00:29:00,363 --> 00:29:02,490
[grunting]

364
00:29:09,664 --> 00:29:10,790
Get on the boat now.

365
00:29:15,462 --> 00:29:16,921
You need to go and help them.

366
00:29:21,718 --> 00:29:22,886
[man] Is it just you?

367
00:29:23,470 --> 00:29:24,721
Where are all the others?

368
00:29:40,236 --> 00:29:41,070
Aunt Becca?

369
00:29:42,739 --> 00:29:45,283
We can't leave here without Sabina!

370
00:29:46,951 --> 00:29:47,994
Huh?

371
00:29:48,077 --> 00:29:49,954
[eerie music playing]

372
00:29:56,961 --> 00:29:58,880
[panting]

373
00:30:22,612 --> 00:30:24,989
[branches creaking]

374
00:30:43,800 --> 00:30:46,135
[rumbling]

375
00:30:51,057 --> 00:30:52,183
[echoing breaths]

376
00:30:57,480 --> 00:30:59,983
[thumping]

377
00:31:18,626 --> 00:31:19,460
[gasps]

378
00:31:21,087 --> 00:31:22,338
Ma!

379
00:31:22,422 --> 00:31:23,339
Sabina.

380
00:31:24,090 --> 00:31:25,008
Please, listen.

381
00:31:26,217 --> 00:31:27,802
It's me who should stay behind.

382
00:31:33,391 --> 00:31:36,269
The same blood
runs through our veins, Sabina.

383
00:31:36,352 --> 00:31:38,688
I hear the island calling as well.

384
00:31:41,691 --> 00:31:43,401
We share the same blood, don't we?

385
00:31:46,613 --> 00:31:48,281
You're so stubborn, Ma.

386
00:31:49,866 --> 00:31:51,868
Goddamn it! Why do you always have to be?

387
00:31:51,951 --> 00:31:53,411
I'm the one who began it.

388
00:31:53,494 --> 00:31:55,914
- No one started anything.
- And I need to end this now.

389
00:31:56,873 --> 00:31:58,458
Sabina, you need to live.

390
00:32:00,168 --> 00:32:02,170
And Bulak needs you to live as well.

391
00:32:04,505 --> 00:32:06,132
Don't waste your life.

392
00:32:11,596 --> 00:32:13,056
Live your life to the fullest.

393
00:32:13,765 --> 00:32:14,724
I love you, Sabina.

394
00:32:15,642 --> 00:32:17,268
I love you so much.

395
00:32:17,810 --> 00:32:19,437
Oh, my darling girl.

396
00:32:19,520 --> 00:32:21,522
[Sabina sobbing]

397
00:32:22,398 --> 00:32:23,316
Go on now.

398
00:32:23,858 --> 00:32:25,193
Come on. You need to leave.

399
00:32:26,527 --> 00:32:27,445
Go on.

400
00:32:29,989 --> 00:32:30,990
Go, now.

401
00:32:39,374 --> 00:32:41,584
[exhales, sniffles]

402
00:32:50,802 --> 00:32:52,595
Are you coming with me, brother?

403
00:32:56,307 --> 00:32:58,643
[distant low snarling]

404
00:33:02,480 --> 00:33:05,900
[suspenseful music playing]

405
00:33:19,914 --> 00:33:22,375
[branches creaking]

406
00:33:27,588 --> 00:33:30,174
- [branches breaking]
- [creature screeching]

407
00:33:30,258 --> 00:33:32,135
[rumbling]

408
00:33:32,218 --> 00:33:34,387
[creature screeches loudly]

409
00:33:39,392 --> 00:33:40,309
[man] Miss!

410
00:33:41,978 --> 00:33:42,895
Let's go.

411
00:33:44,147 --> 00:33:45,481
They're not coming back.

412
00:33:48,276 --> 00:33:49,485
We'll wait some more.

413
00:33:50,319 --> 00:33:51,821
You swim if you want to go.

414
00:33:55,908 --> 00:33:57,952
We're not leaving until Sabina gets here.

415
00:34:10,298 --> 00:34:13,843
[pensive music playing]

416
00:34:43,206 --> 00:34:44,040
Sabina?

417
00:34:44,832 --> 00:34:46,000
Sabina!

418
00:34:53,591 --> 00:34:54,717
Where's Aunt Becca?

419
00:36:20,678 --> 00:36:22,555
[engine spluttering]

420
00:37:13,856 --> 00:37:14,941
Let's go home.

421
00:38:01,821 --> 00:38:04,115
[man 1] <i>Hey, have some respect</i>
<i>for the dead.</i>

422
00:38:05,741 --> 00:38:06,951
Are you sure he's dead?

423
00:38:08,035 --> 00:38:09,453
If the rumors are true,

424
00:38:11,080 --> 00:38:16,043
theirs is the only family that can both
get in and get out of Babang Yawa.

425
00:38:19,130 --> 00:38:20,089
You know what?

426
00:38:20,715 --> 00:38:23,175
Babang Yawa is nothing more than a myth.

427
00:38:23,884 --> 00:38:24,802
Come on.

428
00:38:25,678 --> 00:38:27,388
Every myth starts from the truth.

429
00:38:28,389 --> 00:38:30,474
It depends what you believe after that.

430
00:38:31,058 --> 00:38:34,270
You know, sometimes
you're a real arrogant prick.

431
00:38:36,022 --> 00:38:37,523
Yeah, look who's talking.

432
00:38:37,606 --> 00:38:39,984
[groans] I need to take a piss anyway.

433
00:38:47,658 --> 00:38:50,786
[blows nose]

434
00:39:09,347 --> 00:39:10,264
[burps]

435
00:39:11,974 --> 00:39:13,100
[sighs]

436
00:39:17,313 --> 00:39:20,566
[wings flapping]

437
00:39:24,111 --> 00:39:25,363
[exhales]

438
00:39:25,446 --> 00:39:26,655
[metal squeaking]

439
00:39:30,826 --> 00:39:31,952
[thuds]

440
00:39:34,789 --> 00:39:36,123
[metal clanks]

441
00:39:42,963 --> 00:39:45,674
[suspenseful music playing]

442
00:39:45,758 --> 00:39:47,009
[loud thud]

443
00:39:47,093 --> 00:39:48,302
[growls]

444
00:39:56,352 --> 00:39:57,269
[grunts]

445
00:40:01,899 --> 00:40:04,568
[creature snarling]

446
00:40:04,652 --> 00:40:06,278
[pants]

447
00:40:15,788 --> 00:40:18,332
[theme music playing]
